7e537688aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508945 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508945 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164545" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508945 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508945 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=-z,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508945 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77084529-91b2-5a0f-94a4-b8df58237bc4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508945 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4pz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis and $p=-\\frac{1}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508993 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508993 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164405" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508993 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508993 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the surface $z=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508993 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ec111185-2cdb-5c2e-acc4-77d77fc0a299" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508993 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the equation of an elliptic paraboloid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an elliptic paraboloid with $a=\\sqrt{2},\\,b=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508999 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508999 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164478" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508999 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508999 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n25(x-1)^{2}+16(y-2)^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <z<\\infty \n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508999 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fcd8e2d4-6c09-5241-9d34-1a3c5fb626c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508999 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the equation of an elliptic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand an elliptic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is parallel to the $z$-axis and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ in the $xy$-plane, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an elliptic cylinder with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0})=(1,2),\\,a=\\frac{1}{5},\\,b=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
